// Multi-target debuff zone at a target point (sheet range 120ft -> 37m, a 40-foot cube
// approximated as a 6m-radius sphere -- Cube is not a real GroundAoe shape here, same
// approximation already used for erupting_earth.ron in this folder). "Move sluggishly and react
// far slower" maps onto the existing Slowed buff (generic movement slow) -- an exact fit.
//
// `pooled_debuff` is a shared-HP-budget mechanism built for `Sleep`'s "weakest targets first"
// semantics (`combat::resolve_pooled_debuff_targets`) -- there is no ungated "apply this buff to
// everyone in the radius" GroundAoe path in this engine. `pool` is set generously above any
// plausible in-radius total HP at this level band so the budget realistically never runs out
// before every target in the zone is caught, approximating "creatures in the area" rather than
// gating to the weakest few. No wisdom-save-for-immunity system exists, so the save is dropped
// (matches this folder's other pooled_debuff use in spike_growth.ron: `chance` stays 1.0, the
// pool math is the only gate). Tune the pool value once real mob HP bands are measured.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 80.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    delay: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 37.0,
    radius: 6.0,
    min_falloff: 0.4,
    damage: 0.0,
    poise: 0.0,
    knockback: (strength: 0.0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: No,
    reagent: None,
    rooted_cast: false,
    pooled_debuff: Some((
        pool: 90.0,
        buff: (
            kind: Slowed,
            dur_secs: 60,
            strength: Value(0.5),
            chance: 1.0,
        ),
    )),
    meta: (school: Some(Transmutation), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(25.0)),
)
